<title>JAPAN: Japan buys 160,000 tonnes wheat, 60,000 T barley.</title>
<headline>Japan buys 160,000 tonnes wheat, 60,000 T barley.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Japanese Food Agency said on Thursday it had bought 120,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat, 20,000 tonnes of Canadian wheat, 20,000 tonnes of Australian wheat, 20,000 tonnes of Canadian barley and 40,000 tonnes of Australian barley at its weekly tender.</p>
<p>All purchases were for May shipment.</p>
<p>The tender results details are as follows, in tonnes.</p>
<p>WHEAT</p>
<p>    Country    Quantity</p>
<p>    U.S.	 120,000	  Western white	    28,000</p>
<p>					Dark northern spring   40,000</p>
<p>					Hard red winter	  20,000</p>
<p>					(13 percent protein)   20,000</p>
<p>					 (Ordinary)		12,000</p>
<p>    Canada     20,000	   1 Canadian western red spring</p>
<p>									5,000</p>
<p>					Durum			15,000</p>
<p>    Australia  20,000	   Standard white	   20,000</p>
<p>BARLEY</p>
<p>    Country    Quantity</p>
<p>    Canada     20,000	   Feed			 20,000</p>
<p>    Australia  40,000	   Feed			 40,000</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodity Desk, +81-3-3432-7431</p>
</text>
